## Setup

Install [Homebrew](https://brew.sh) (or see <https://mise.jdx.dev> on Linux), then run in the
repository:

```sh
brew install mise gh
mise trust && mise install    # Go and golangci-lint, versions from mise.toml
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
go install golang.org/x/tools/gopls@{{gopls_version}}   # optional: editor support
gh extension install github/gh-stack                    # optional: stacked PRs
```

mise installs the exact Go and golangci-lint versions in `mise.toml`, checked against the
checksums in `mise.lock`. To get `go` on your `PATH`, activate mise in your shell
(<https://mise.jdx.dev/getting-started.html>), or prefix commands with `mise exec --`.
`scripts/check` finds the pinned tools by itself. On Linux, the race detector also needs a C
compiler (gcc). The git hook runs the checks before each push.

In your editor, leave gopls on plain gofmt. `golangci-lint fmt` is the formatter of record, and
two gofumpt versions can disagree.

## Commands

```sh
scripts/check                       # every quality gate: format, modules, lint, build, test
go build ./...
go test -race ./...
go run ./cmd/{{package}}
golangci-lint fmt                   # format
```

`scripts/check` is the single list of gates. The git hook and CI run it too. The weekly
`explore` workflow runs the tests in random order with new property inputs, and govulncheck.

AI agents follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). Reviews apply [CODING_STANDARDS.md](CODING_STANDARDS.md).
